{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4sikTx46k8HNeSKDR2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient oak, iron-banded, weathered by centuries of hands pressing against its grain.*\n\n*A single keyhole glints dully in the half-light.*\n\n*You hold a key.*\n\n*But which key? The word alone is not enough. A key must have teeth. A key must have shape. A key must know the lock it was cut for.*\n\n*The keyhole waits, dark and patient as a pupil.*\n\n*I do not open.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":111,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}